Latchet.; Corrigia.

@AC 1748. "If from a string even to a latchet of a shoe" (Genesis 14:23) = all things which were unclean natural and corporeal. Explained... By "the string of a shoe" is signified what is false; and by "the latchet of a shoe," what is evil; and this the lowest of all, because it is in the diminutive.

@--[end]. This was meant by John the Baptist, when he said, "There cometh One stronger than I; the latchet of Whose shoes I am not worthy to unloose."

Late.; Serotinus. @AE 376[9]. @644[8]. @--[15]. @--[21].

Latent. See <Hidden, To lie>.

Lateral. See <Side-Latus>.

