@466[end]. Not at all with those who from causes legitimate...

@467. That concubinage apart from a wife, when it takes place from causes legitimate, just, and truly weighty, is not unlawful -illicitus-. General article.

@468. That the legitimate causes of this concubinage are the legitimate causes of divorce, when the wife is nevertheless retained at home. General article.

Lawgiver.; Legislator.

@AC 6372. "And a lawgiver from between his feet" (Genesis 49:10) = the truths which are from (the Celestial Kingdom) in lower things. "A lawgiver" = truths.

@--[2]. For at that time the Celestial Kingdom exercised its Power through the truth (which is from good); and as this was the case, this truth is called "a lawgiver." This truth is also understood by "a lawgiver" in (the following passages). Illustrated @6584[end].

@SE 4432[end]. He who acts against just laws... throws the blame upon the lawgiver...

@AE 355[33]. "The lawgivers of Israel" (Judges 5:9) = the truths of the Church.

@433[4]. "And a lawgiver from between his feet" (Genesis 49:10) = that the truth of the Word (shall not recede) from its ultimate sense.

@435[8]. "For there is the portion of the hidden lawgiver" (Deuteronomy 33:21) = the truths Divine which lie hidden therein.

@440[5]. The reason Judah is called Jehovah's "lawgiver" (Psalms 60:7; 108[8]), is that by "Judah" is signified internal Divine truth, or the Word in the spiritual sense; and the like by "lawgiver," and "law."

@447[4]. "Lawgivers" (Judges 5:14) = those who are in truths from good; and, abstractedly, the truths of good.

@537[3]. A "lawgiver" (Numbers 21:18) = the Lord as to the Word, and as to doctrine from the Word. @AC 3424[end].

