@9174. To "ask a loan" (Exodus 22:14) = truth from another stock. Explained.

@9176. The truths which have with them their own good, are meant by "the things lent..."

@9210[4]. To lend truths, or instruct, for the sake of gain. Signified.

Lend.; Mutuo dare.

@AC 9049[6]. To "lend" = to instruct.

@9174[3]. To "lend" = to instruct from the affection of charity. Illustrated.

@--[4]. To "lend" (Luke 6:34) = to do good from the affection of charity, thus to communicate the goods of Heaven, and also the goods of the world; but the latter for the sake of the former as the end.

@9209. To "lend" (Exodus 22:25) = from the affection of charity to communicate the goods of Heaven; thus to instruct.

@9213[4]. To "lend" (Deuteronomy 24:10) = the communication of truth.

@AE 559[7]. "He shall lend to thee, and thou shalt not lend to him" (Deuteronomy 28:44) = that he shall teach thee truths, but thou shalt not teach him.

@695[7]. To "lend" (Luke 6:35) = to communicate the goods and truths of doctrine from the Word.

Length.; Longitudo.
Long.; Longus.

@AC 650. That "the length" = the holiness of these things... cannot be so well confirmed from the Word, because everything is predicated according to the subject treated of; as, for instance, "length," in application to time, = what is perpetual and eternal; as "length of days;" but in application to space, it = what is holy...

@788[end]. As a tall man. @1126. @SE 4072.

@1613. "According to its length, and according to its breadth" (Genesis 13:17) = what is celestial and spiritual; or, what is the same, good and truth.

@--. The Celestial, or good, being primary, is compared to length; and the Spiritual, or truth, being secondary, is compared to breadth. Illustrated.

@3527[end]. For length, and the things which are of length, are predicated of good.

@4482. (Therefore) lengths, breadths, and heights, which are measurements of space, = such things as are of state; length = what is holy; height, what is good; and breadth, what is true. References. @--[end].

@8898[end]. That "length" is said of good. References.

@9487. "Two cubits and a half its length" (Exodus 25:10) = all as to good.

@--[2]. That "length," in the Word, = good; and "breadth," truth. Explained.

@--. The measuring of the New Jerusalem as to "length" = the quality of good; and as to "breadth," the quality of truth.

@9529. "Two cubits its length" (Exodus 25:23) = all as to conjunction with good.

@9600. "The length of one curtain eight and twenty in cubit" (Exodus 26:2) = what is holy of truth from good. "Length" = good.

@9617. "The length of one curtain thirty in cubit" (Exodus 26:8) = what is full of truth from good. "Length" = good.

@9636. "Ten cubits the length of a board" (Exodus 26:16) = that this good is all in all... "Length" = good; here, the supporting good, which is the good of merit...

@9716. "Five cubits the length, and five cubits the breadth" (Exodus 27:1) = equally from good and from truth.

@9745. "A hundred in cubit the length" (Exodus 27:9) = full with good from the Lord. Explained.

@9750. "Length" = good. @9751. @9862. @10179. @AE 627[4]. @675[15].

@9771. "The length of the court a hundred in cubit" (Exodus 27:18) = the good of that Heaven to the full.

@10179. The reason "length" = good, is that these things are reckoned from the east to the west; and by the east and west is signified good from one terminus to the other.

@10181[2]. Under <Degree>, see this reference.

@HH 168[end]. Times seem long to those who are sad... @AE 1219[4].

@197[2]. I will state what is signified in the Word by "length," "breadth," and "height." In the world, that is called long and broad which is long and broad as to space; in like manner what is high; but in Heaven, where they do not think from space, by length is meant a state of good; by breadth, a state of truth; and by height, the differences in them according to degrees... because long, in Heaven, is from east to west; and there are those who are in the good of love: and broad, in Heaven, is from south to north; and there are those who are in truth from good: and high, in Heaven, is both according to degrees. Hence it is, that in the Word, by "length," "breadth," and "height," such things are signified. Illustrated. @AR 861[2].

@--[3]. "The length" of the New Jerusalem = its good of love; its "breadth," the truth from that good; and its "height," the good and truth as to degrees.

@NJHD 1[5]. "Length" = good and its extension; and "breadth" = truth and its extension. References.

@DLW 71. In all the objects of (natural) sight there is figure derived from what is long, broad, and high...

@--[2]. But the thought of an Angel has nothing in common with the figure... which derives anything from what Is long, broad, and high of space; but from the state of a thing from the state of the life. Hence, instead of what is long of space, he thinks of the good of a thing from the good of life; instead of what is broad of space, of the truth of a thing from the truth of life; and instead of height, of the degrees of these. Thus he thinks from correspondence... from which correspondence it is that "length," in the Word, = the good of a thing; "breadth," the truth of a thing; and "height," the degrees of these.

@AR 906. "Its length is as great as its breadth" (Revelation 21:16) = that the good and truth in that Church make one, as do essence and form. By "the length" of the city Jerusalem, is signified the good of the Church; and by its "breadth" is signified the truth of the Church. Explained.

@907. "The length, and the breadth, and the height of it were equal" (Revelation 21:16) = that all things of it were from the good of love... For by "length" is signified the good of love... and this precedes, the others being "equal" to it.

@AE 600[12]. "Long" = extension.

@629[4]. "Length" = the good of the Church.

@--[6]. "Length" = its good of love.

@654[20]. They are called "men of length" (Isaiah 45:14) from good; for "length" = good and its quality.

Lentil.; Lens.

@AC 3332. "Pulse of lentils" (Genesis 25:34) = the good of doctrinal things... "Lentils" = the good of them. @3941[5].

Leopard.; Pardus. Leopardus.

@AC 430. "The leopard" (Isaiah 11:6) = the opposite (to the second degree of innocence). ( = the genuine truth of the Church falsified. @AR 572[end].) @AE 314[3].

@3540. As these truths and goods are from evil, they are compared to... "the leopard," and "its spots" (Jeremiah 13:23).

@6441[end]. Mentioned.

@AR 572. "The beast I saw was like a leopard" (Revelation 13:2) = a heresy destructive of the Church, because from the truths of the Word falsified... By "a leopard" is signified the affection or cupidity of falsifying the truths of the Word; and, as it is a ferocious beast, and slaughters harmless animals, it signifies also a heresy destructive of the Church. The reason the falsified truths of the Word are signified by "a leopard," is from its black and white spots; and by the black spots are signified falsities, and by the white among them, truth. Hence, as it is a ferocious and fierce beast, by it are signified the truths of the Word falsified, and thus destroyed. Illustrated.

@574. That "the leopard," "bear," and "lion" = such things, may be evident from the like beasts seen by Daniel (Daniel 7:3-7). By these four beasts are described the successive states of the Church... The third state of it is described by "the leopard," by which is signified the Word falsified as to its truths; by "the four wings, like those of birds, upon its back," are signified confirmations of falsity...

@CL 44[4]. Before the eyes of the Angels they appear with feet like those of calves, or leopards.

@78[2]. Bears were seen on the left, and leopards on the right, (which) were men who guard those inhabitants of the north, and who rush at all who are spiritual. Those who... confirm falsities thence, appear afar as leopards.

@79[2]. We saw dragons and leopards, such as are described in Revelation 13:2... Their Falsities, and depraved inclinations towards the things which are of worship, are represented by the dragons and leopards.

@231[5]. They appeared... like graven images of stone clothed with leopard's skins. @TCR 185[2].

@TCR 13[end]. They become... leopards as to deceit.

@324[end]. Such are described in the Word by "leopards."

@381[end]. They appear as to their eyes like leopards.

@569[4]. A devil who appeared from afar like a leopard...

@AE 355[24]. Their cupidity of perverting truths and destroying them through reasonings from falsities entirely remote from truths, is signified by, "his horses are swifter than leopards" (Habakkuk 1:8).

@780. "The beast I saw was like a leopard" = reasonings which disagree but which still appear to cohere... "A leopard" = things which disagree, and which yet appear as true. The reason such things are signified by "a leopard," is that a leopard has its skin marked off and variegated with spots, from which variegation it appears not unbeautiful; but as it is a fierce and insidious animal, and above all others swift in seizing its prey; and as those also are such who are skilled in reasoning expertly to confirm the dogma concerning the separation of faith from good works, by means of reasonings from the natural man, which, notwithstanding its disagreement with truths, they thereby make to appear as if it cohered with them = therefore as to its body this beast appeared like a leopard. Example(s). @--[5]. Illustrated.

@--[5]. "Or the leopard his spots" = that neither can the falsity of evil change; "the leopard," here, = the falsity of evil; for it = truth falsified by means of reasonings; and "spots" = things falsified.

@--[6]. "The leopard" (Isaiah 11) = the falsity which is opposite to charity; and which, by means of reasonings in favour of faith, endeavours to destroy charity.

@--[7]. "The leopard is awake against their cities" (Jeremiah 5:6) = reasonings from the falsities of evil against the truths of doctrine.

@--[8]. "Whose horses are swifter than leopards" = the cupidity of seducing by means of reasonings, and the consequent expertness in seducing... Reasonings from the natural man are signified by... "leopards."

@--[9]. "The leopard," in Daniel 7, also = reasonings which disagree, but which still appear as if they cohere.

@--[10]. "As a leopard upon the way will I observe" (Hosea 13:7) = the falsification of truth by means of reasonings from the natural man. By "a leopard" is signified falsification by means of reasonings... This is so said concerning the Lord... from the appearance of truth... for it is the man himself who falsifies truth by means of reasonings, when he is elated at heart.

@1200[3]. (The leopard included among animals of an intermediate character, which appear in the World of Spirits.)

@TCRAdd 9. 8. Those [Spirits] who are like leopards, smell those who are crafty.

Leprosy.; Lepra.
Leprous. Leper.; Leprosus.

@AC 3301[8]. That in leprosy the colours of the hair and beard were to be observed; as white, reddish, yellow, black; and also in the garments; and that he who was cleansed from leprosy was to shave off all the hair of his head, beard, and eyebrows (Leviticus 13:1-59; 14:8, 9) signified falsities unclean from what is profane, which is "leprosy" in the internal sense.

@6959[3]. As "leprosy" = the profanation of truth...

@6963. "His hands as leprous as snow" (Exodus 4:6) = the profanation of truth. "Hands" = ... truth; and "leprous" = profanation; in special, the profanation of truth.

@--. The reason "leprosy" is so much treated of, is... that it signified the profanation of truth... and because the Jews and Israelites could profane truth more than others...

@--[3]. That "leprosy" = the profanation of truth, is evident from the statutes concerning leprosy in Leviticus 13. In this description there is contained in the internal sense every quality of the profanation of truth, Enumerated. But as the things described by "leprosy" are profane, it is not allowable to explain them particularly...

@--[4]. "One who is leprous from the head to the heel" (Leviticus 13:12-14) means one who knows internal truths, but does not acknowledge them... He is not interiorly in profanation, but exteriorly, which is removed; and therefore he is "clean." But if he knows the truths of faith, and believes them, and yet lives contrary to them... he is in profanation interiorly; and so is he who has believed, and afterwards denies; and therefore it is said that "in the day in which living flesh has appeared in him he shall be unclean"...

@7524[3]. The sores of the leprosy... mentioned in Leviticus 13, are also such (falsities); for "leprosy" = the profanation of truth.

@9014[5]. "He who is leprous" (2 Samuel 3:29) = the profanation of the truth of faith.

@9209[4]. "The lepers are cleansed" (Luke 7:22)... "The lepers" = those who are unclean, and who still long to be cleansed.

@9468[9]. For "leprosy" = truth profaned, thus falsified.

@AR 678[end]. As the Jewish nation was in the profanation of the Word, and this is signified by "leprosy," they had leprosy not only in their flesh, but also in their garments, houses, and vessels; and the kinds of profanation are signified by the various evils of the leprosy, Enumerated, @AE 962[10].

@CL 264. The face (of the devil) was leprous from his forehead to his chin; and also both his hands.

@TCR 148[2]. She infects them with her leprosy.

@WE 6416. Leprosy treated of, and Explained. @WE 5555. @WE 5559. @WE 5560. @WE 5565. @WE 5600. @WE 5605. @WE 5616. @WE 5621. @WE 5640.

@AE 475[18]. By "Naaman the leper" was represented those who falsify... For "leprosy" = falsifications. (The curing of his leprosy Fully Explained.)

@600[19]. As by "leprosy" is signified good consumed through falsities, the method of the restoration of this evil by Divine means is described by the process of the cleansing of the leprosy... in Leviticus 14:14-28...

@962[10]. As by "leprosy" is signified the profanation of truth, and the profanation of truth is various - being light and grievous, interior and exterior, and being according to the quality of the profaned truth - its effects are various, which are signified by the appearances in the leprosy, Enumerated.

