@8663. "He bowed himself" = a letting in, or immission. @8666[end].

@10286. By light let in from Heaven.

@HH 348. They introduce Divine truths immediately into the life.

@482[2]. For all are let into their own loves...

@491[end]. They are taken out of these caverns, and sent into them, by turns.

@502. He is let into the state of his interiors. @504. @--[end]. @531[2]. @--[end]. @551[2].

@551[end]. Vastation is nothing else than a letting into the internals...

@553[4]. As soon as any light of Heaven is let in...

@558[2]. Man is let into his proprium, whenever...

@--. Skilled in the art of letting upright Spirits into their proprium... by this - that they let them into thoughts about themselves.

@LJ 50[end]. No one can be withdrawn from his religiosity unless he is first let into it.

@DP 164[5]. Every man is from infancy inserted into this divine man.

@221. That man is not interiorly let into truths... and goods... except in so far as he can be kept in them... General article. @232. @AE 1158[2].

@222. That a man can be let into the wisdom of spiritual things, and also into the love of them, and still not be reformed. General article.

@CL 48. a. [3]. To this end he is let into his external and into his internal by turns...

@TCR 614. He was let into his Own sins...

@AE 503[4]. "A sending of angels of evil" (Psalms 78:49) = the falsity of evil from Hell.

Lethargy.; Lethargia. @TCR 497, @509, @619[3].

Lethargy.; Veternus. @CL 207[3].

