Letter.; Litera.
Letter, little.; Literula.
See <Hebrew letters>, see <Hebrew language>.
See also <A (the letter, sounded as in father)>, <B (the letter)>, <E (the letter, sounded like the a in Fate)>, <H (the letter)>, <I (the letter, sounded as in pique)>, <N (the Letter)>, <O (the letter)>, <U (the letter, sounded oo, as in rule)>, <Y (the letter)>; and also see <Epistle>, <Sense of the letter>, <Syllable>, and <Write>.

@AC 7236[end]. From only twenty-three letters, put together in different ways, there can arise the words of all languages.

@BE 81. To be sent down from heaven engraven in silver characters, @TCR 181.

@TCR 615[end]. It becomes in the mouth that repeats it a sound of so many letters.

@SE 159. And when I am writing letters.

@AC 1870[2]. Inspired as to each of the little letters...

@9280[end]. Holiness inflows... into the literal sense, and into the letter itself.

@DSS 3. The holiness of the Word... in some places is in the letters themselves.

@71. The spiritual style consists of mere letters, each of which involves a meaning; and there are points over the letters, which exalt the meaning. The letters with the Angels of the Spiritual Kingdom are like the printed letters in our world; and the letters with the Angels of the Celestial Kingdom - each of which also involves a complete meaning - are like the old Hebrew letters... @DLW 295.

@DP 230. (In the spiritual language) each letter in the alphabet means one thing; and a number of letters joined together into one word... involve the entire state of the thing. @AR 29[2]. @--. @TCR 19[end].

@AR 38[2]. As, in the Spiritual World... each letter means a thing, David wrote Psalms 119 in order, according to the letters of the alphabet... Something like this appears in Psalms 111.

@TCR 241. The letters with the Angels of the Celestial Kingdom, with some, are like the Arabic letters; with some are like the old Hebrew letters; but they are inflected above and within, with signatures above, between, and within. Each of these, also, involves a complete meaning.

@508[end]. As the paper was written with rounded -circinatis- letters, such as are in that Heaven, I... begged that they would explain (it).

@SE 3503[2]. They do not remain in the letter; but in the interior sense of the letter.

@5561. In the Spiritual Heaven, the writing is in... Roman letters... @5579.

@5562. But in the Celestial Heaven... the letters are... almost like the Hebrew letters; and there they see in each of the syllables, little horns, and apexes, many things which they signify.

@5563. They write letters, and send them to others.

@5621. (Thus) the Word is Divine in the syllables and letters also... (Hence) the Jews were driven to count the letters; and they have believed that there are arcana in the several letters; although they did not know how.

@5951. Under <England>, see this reference.

@5965. In Heaven... the letters of the words are sometimes written by curvatures, which also contain arcana...

@DMin 4778. Letters printed with type seen there.

@4778. They have both written, and as it were printed, letters... But I did not understand the language...

@AE 260[2]. If the Word were spiritual in the letter also, there would be no basis for it, and it would be like a house without a foundation.

@828[3]. (The Angels of the Third Heaven) do not write by means of letters, as do the other Angels; but by means of curvatures and inflections which contain arcana...

@1070[end]. The Word in the letter, which is with us, is Divine truth in ultimates.

@Ath 112[end]. Hence the Word in the letter is most holy... and strength itself is there.

@LJPost 261. The Word in the (old Hebrew) letter has more immediate communication with Heaven.

@LJPost 332. Spirits and Angels... write by means of letters and characters; but the writing is quite different from that in the world, except the letters and some of the points...

@LJPost 332[end]. They write the meanings of words by means of alphabetical letters, each of which signifies a thing...

@DeVerbo 3[7]. As to the letters, the writing of the spiritual Angels is like the writing of men in the world; but each letter signifies a thing; so that if you were to see it when in a natural state you would say that it is mere letters. But in the highest Heaven the writings are not the same as to the letters; they have letters written by means of various curvatures, not unlike the letters of the Hebrew language, but everywhere inflected, and not merely linear... Each letter involves a thing, the perception of which they have from affection, and not from thought.

@14[2]. But the writing of the celestial Word is from letters unknown in the world. They are indeed alphabetical letters; but each [is formed] from inflected lines, with little horns above and below; and there are jots or points in the letters, and also below and above them. It was said that such was the writing with the Most Ancients in this Earth...

@14[4]. The writing of the spiritual Word is from letters which are like the printed letters in our world; but each letter makes a meaning: and therefore if you were to see that writing, you would not understand a single word; for letter is placed next to letter in a continuous series, with little lines and points above and below; for it is according to the spiritual speech...

@22. In very many places it is better for man to understand the Word according to the letter. Example(s), Explained.

@24. Under <Word>, see this reference.

@26[3]. (In order to express "horses harnessed to a chariot," the spiritual Angels) write only "I;" and this letter expresses it... They also write "the understanding of doctrine" by means of "I;" but they are then in higher thought; from which it was evident that there are correspondences in the words of their language.

@DWis 7. 5. 3. Although as to the letters the writing of the Angels is like the writings of the men of the world. It cannot be understood by any man of the world; [because] every consonant letter therein is one meaning; and every vowel letter is an affection. The vowel letters are not written, but are pointed.

Letter (of the Word). See <Sense of the letter>; and also see <Letter>.

Level, To.; Applanare. @TCR 73[2].

Levi.; Levi.
See <Levite>.

@AC 342. "Levi" = charity; and therefore the tribe of Levi received the priesthood, and represented "the shepherd of the flock."

@352. (Hence) the tribe of Levi - who in the internal sense - love - was accepted in place of all the first-born, and was made the priesthood (Numbers 3:40-46; 8:14-20).

@1038[3]. "Levi," in the supreme sense, = the Lord; and thence the man who has love and charity; and therefore "the covenant of lives and of peace with Levi" (Malachi 2:4, 5) = [that] in love and charity. @1286[4]. @2826[7].

@3325[9]. As "the first-born" represented the Lord; and those who are the Lord's are so from love to Him, therefore the tribe of Levi was accepted in place of all the first-born; and this because Levi represented the Lord as to love. "Levi" also = love; for Levi means adhesion and conjunction...

@3759[end]. These four degrees are signified by... Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah.

@3858[11]. The tribe of Levi = love... Hence the rod of Levi only blossomed (Numbers 17).

@3861[end]. Levi was so called from "adhering." @3875[6]. @AR 357.

@3862[3]. By "Levi" is signified spiritual love, or charity.

@--. The progression is thence... to charity, which is "Levi"...

@3869[2]. Faith in the will, when it becomes charity, is "Levi."

@3870[2]. "Levi" (here) = an affection contrary to charity.

@3875[4]. Those who are in spiritual love are called "sons of Levi" (Malachi 3:3).

@--. That, in the supreme sense, the Lord is "Levi," from His Divine love and mercy towards those who are in spiritual love (is evident from) Malachi 2:4-9.

@--. And as the Divine love or mercy of the Lord is meant, in the supreme sense, by "Levi;" and, in the internal sense, spiritual love; therefore the tribe of Levi was made the priesthood...

@--[5]. This mutual love, or charity towards the neighbour, is what is meant by spiritual love, and is what is signified by "Levi."

@3877. "She called his name Levi" (Genesis 29:34) = its quality... This quality is what is signified by "Levi," and also by the tribe named from him; and it is this third universal of the Church, or the third universal when man is being regenerated... and it is charity. Explained.

@4497. "Simeon and Levi" (Genesis 34:25) = faith and love... "Levi" = spiritual love, or charity. In the genuine sense, these things are signified by Simeon and Levi, and also by the tribes named from Simeon and Levi; but, in the opposite sense, falsity and evil... Relatively to the Jewish nation... Simeon and Levi represent these, (in that) they killed Hamor, Shechem, and the men of the city... Simeon and Levi did this in order that it might be represented that the truth of faith and the good of charity had become falsity and evil... @4499. @4502[2]. @--[3]. Explained.

@4515. To "Simeon and Levi" (Genesis 34:30) = what is representative of spiritual and celestial things... "Levi" = love; but, in the opposite sense, evil; here, therefore, what is representative of... celestial things. Explained.

@4606. Under <Judah>, see this reference.

@--. In the supreme sense, "Levi" = love and mercy; in the internal sense, charity or spiritual love; and, in the external sense, conjunction. References.

@5622[3]. (The blossoming of the almonds) was a sign that the tribe of Levi had been chosen for the priesthood, because by it was signified charity, which is the essential of the Spiritual Church.

@6024. "The sons of Levi, Gershon, Kohath, and Merari" (Genesis 46:2) = spiritual love, and its doctrinal things in general. @7230[2].

@6352. "Simeon and Levi are brethren" (Genesis 49:5) = faith in the will, and charity; here, what is contrary, because [they = ] faith separated from charity. Explained.

@--[end]. Therefore, by "Levi" is represented evil in act; for this is opposite to charity.

@6716. "There went a man of the house of Levi" (Exodus 2:1) = the origin of truth from good... "Levi" represents good; for, in the supreme sense, "Levi" represents the Divine love; and, in the internal sense, spiritual love; and, as he represents love, he represents good; for all good is of love.

@6717. "And took a daughter of Levi" (Exodus 2:1) = conjunction with good. Explained.

@7184. Afterwards (in Exodus 6) there is described the Lord's Spiritual Kingdom as to faith and as to charity... Levi and his families represent the things which are of charity.

@7230[3]. "These are the families of Levi according to their births" (Exodus 6:19) = that these things are goods and truths from charity.

@7231. The reason why Reuben, Simeon, and Levi, and their sons, are here mentioned, and not the rest of the fathers of the tribes with their sons. Explained.

@--[2]. Finally, in the (new) will (of the man of the Spiritual Church) there is apperceived the affection of charity; so that he wills to do what is good, not, as before, from faith, but from charity towards the neighbour... It is this charity with its affection which is represented by Levi.

@8093[2]. Faith separated from charity is described by... Simeon and Levi, in that they killed Hamor... and were therefore cursed by their father.

@8159[2]. "The sons of Levi" (Malachi 3) = those who are of the Spiritual Church; for by "Levi" is signified charity, or spiritual good. @9293[end].

@10484[end]. "The sons of Levi," who congregated to Moses, (Exodus 32:26) = those who are in truths from good, (which is the same as being in charity). @10485. @10491.

@AR 17[7]. "Levi" = truth in act, which is the good of life; and therefore the priesthood was given to his posterity.

@356. By Reuben, Simeon, and Levi... are signified truth in the understanding, or faith; truth in the will, or charity; and truth in act, or good work; the like as by Peter, James, and John.

@357. "From the tribe of Levi were sealed twelve thousand" (Revelation 7:7) = the affection of truth from good from which is intelligence with those who will be of the Lord's New Heaven and New Church. By "Levi," in the supreme sense, is signified love and mercy; in the spiritual sense, charity in act, which is the good of life; and, in the natural sense, consociation and conjunction; for he was so called from to "adhere," by which... is signified conjunction through love. But here, by "Levi" is signified the love or affection of truth, and the derivative intelligence; because he follows Simeon, and is the middle one in this series. As Levi represented these things, that tribe was made the priesthood. Illustrated. That the tribe of Levi = the love of truth, which is the very love from which the Church is the Church, and the derivative intelligence. Illustrated.

@--[end]. To "purify the sons of Levi" = to purify those who are in the affection of truth. As this affection blossoms from intelligence, the rod of Levi, upon which was written the name of Aaron, blossomed with almonds (Numbers 17:1-11).

@SE 5987. See <Espalier>.

@AE 229[4]. The tribe of Levi was the first of the tribes, because Levi represented the good of charity; and therefore this tribe was made the priesthood, (which) is the first of the Church, References.

@242[9]. "The sons of Levi" = all who are in the good of charity, and thence in the truths of faith...

@340[8]. As the sons of Levi were set over Divine worship, and all Divine worship takes place from spiritual good and from the truths thence, it is said that "Jehovah chose them to minister to Him, and to bless in the name of Jehovah" (Deuteronomy 10:8; 21:5)...

@365[25]. "Levi" = all who are in the good of charity towards the neighbour; and, in the supreme sense, the Lord Himself, because this good is from Him; here, (Malachi 2) the Lord Himself. References.

@438. The obedience of faith is signified by... (the tribes of) Simeon, Levi, and Issachar.

@443. The tribes of Simeon, Levi, and Issachar, who... constitute the third class of the sealed, = those who are in the First Heaven... Explained.

@--[6]. "Simeon and Levi are brethren" = faith separated from charity.

@--[7]. The reason his first three sons, Reuben, Simeon, and Levi, were rejected and condemned by their father Israel, is that in that prophecy it treats of the instauration of the Church... and by "Levi" is there signified no good of charity... Explained.

@444. "From the tribe of Levi were sealed twelve thousand" = good works... because charity consists in the performance of goods. Explained.

@--[3]. The reason the priesthood was given to the tribe of Levi, was that it represented love and charity...

@--[4]. As the tribe of Levi represented charity in act, thus the goods of charity...

@--. As the good of charity must be in all things of the Church... and because the affection itself of good and truth... gives to understand, and instructs all, the tribe of Levi was not only made the priesthood, but there was also no inheritance given to it... (Numbers 35; Joshua 21).

@--[5]. "The sons of Levi" (Deuteronomy 21:5) = the affection of good and truth, which is charity.

@--[6]. That the tribe of Levi = the goods of charity, which are good works. Illustrated.

@--[8]. "The sons of Levi" (Malachi 3) = all who are in the good of charity, and thence in the good of faith. Explained.

@--[8]. By "Levi" (Deuteronomy 33:8-12) is meant the affection of spiritual truth, Explained.

@--[11]. That "Levi" = love and charity. Illustrated.

@--. "Levi" means "adhesion;" and "adhesion" = conjunction through spiritual love.

@--. The three sons of Leah, born in order = Reuben, Simeon, and Levi, = the first and primary essentials of the Church in their series; namely, truth in the understanding, truth in the will, and truth in act; in like manner as the Lord's three disciples...

@--[12]. That "Levi," in the supreme sense, = the Lord as to love and mercy, is evident from... Malachi 2. By "Levi," here, in the supreme sense, is meant the Lord as to the Divine Human. Explained... And therefore by "the covenant of Levi" is meant conjunction with the Lord through love and charity, @696[16], @701[9].

@--[13]. "Levi," and his tribe, in the opposite sense, = the evil of falsity, which is opposite to the good of charity; and also life without charity, consequently, no charity towards the neighbour. Illustrated.

@494[end]. "The sons of Levi" (Deuteronomy 33) = those who are in the truths of spiritual good.

@555[10]. "Levi" (Zechariah 12. 13) = the good of charity.

@701[9]. For the Lord is meant by "Levi," as He is by "David;" but by "Levi," as to the Divine good, which is the Lord's priestly [office], Explained.

Leviathan.; Leviathan.

@AC 7293[2]. As "whales" = scientifics which pervert the truths of faith, they = reasonings from fallacies, whence come falsities... Like things are signified by "leviathan" in Isaiah 27:1; and in Psalms 74:14.

@--[3]. In a good sense, "leviathan" = reason from truths (Job 41:1-26). Reason from truths is the opposite to reasonings from falsities, @9755[4].

@10416[end]. "Leviathan" = the Scientific in general.

@BE 93[end]. I said. You are also leviathans... the crooked leviathans... and the longish leviathans... @TCR 182[end].

@TCR 74[2]. I said... Open that faith, and you will see... leviathan...

@AE 275[3]. "Leviathan the longish serpent" (Isaiah 27:1) = those who reject all things which they do not see with their eyes; thus the merely sensuous, who are devoid of faith because they do not comprehend. "Leviathan the crooked serpent" (Isaiah 27:1) = those who on this account do not believe, and yet say that they believe.

@455[18]. Under <Behemoth>, see this reference.

@483[end]. "Whales" and "leviathan" (Psalms 74) = scientifics, which are of the sensuous and natural man, from which is all falsity, when the spiritual man is closed above them.

@514[11]. By "leviathan," that is, a whale, (Psalms 104:26) are meant all things of the natural man in the complex; which is said to "play in the sea," from the delight of knowing and thence of being wise.

@581[8]. Their cunning is signified by "leviathan the crooked serpent."

Levirate.; Leviratus.

@AC 1748[4]. The levirate mentioned. @4818[2].

@4834. The levirate represented the preservation and continuation of the Church.

@4835. "Perform the levirate to her" (Genesis 38:8) = that he should continue the representative of the Church... To "perform the levirate" = to preserve and continue that which is of the Church. The levirate defined. It was not new in the Jewish Church...

@--[2]. The law of the levirate quoted (Deuteronomy 25:5-10).

@--[3]. The signification of the law of the levirate explained. @--[4].

@4836. Not to perform the levirate = not to want the good and truth of the Church, and its continuation.

Levite.; Levita.
See <Levi>.

@AC 2252[4]. The Levites numbered from 30 to 50 years. Explained.

@2276[4]. The Levites taken for the ministry at 30. Explained. @5335[2]. @--[3].

@3325[9]. The Levites given to Aaron. Explained.

@6998. "Is not Aaron the Levite thy brother?" (Exodus 4:14) = the doctrine of good and truth... Aaron is called "the Levite," because by "a Levite" is signified the doctrine of good and truth of the Church, which ministers and is of service to the priesthood.

@8080[2]. The Levites were accepted in place of the firstborn, because by Levi was represented the good of faith, or charity, (Numbers 3:12-51; 8:16-18). That the good of faith is that which is to be ascribed to the Lord... @--[4].

@9959[4]. "The priests the Levites" (Ezekiel 44:15) = those who are in truths from good.

@10017. The priesthood which is represented by the Levites, is the Lord's work of salvation proceeding from this again. (See <Aaron>.)

@--[2]. The work of the salvation of those who are thence in natural good, is represented by the priesthood of the Levites... and therefore it is said concerning the Levites that they were "given to Aaron" (Numbers 3).

@10083[2]. The Levites represented truths ministering to good; and Aaron, the good to which they ministered; and therefore the Levites were "agitated" (Numbers 8:11-21); that is, vivified. Therefore, also, it is said that they are to be "purified," Explained.

@10093[3]. As the Levites represented the Divine truths in Heaven and in the Church being of service to Divine good, they were given to Aaron in place of all the firstborn...

@AR 17[7]. See <"First-born">.

@AE 444[7]. "The Levites" (Jeremiah 33:18) = those who are in worship (from the good of love and of charity, and from the truths of faith)... "The Levites the priests, My ministers" (Jeremiah 33:21) = those who are in the good of love to the Lord, and in the derivative worship... "Thus will I multiply... the Levites My ministers" (Jeremiah 33:22) = the fructification of Divine good with those who have conjunction with the Lord. Here, as elsewhere, by "the Levites, the priests," are signified those who are in the good of love and of charity; and, in the abstract sense, this good. @527[5].

@--[14]. This opposite is signified by "the Levite," in the parable... (Luke 10:32)... "The Levite" = those who have no charity towards the neighbour, such as there were in Jerusalem at that time.

@710[34]. The Levites were received in place of all the first-born, because by "Levi," and thence by "a Levite," is signified spiritual good from celestial good; and therefore the priesthood, by which is signified celestial good, was given to Aaron and his sons; and the ministry of this good, by which is signified truth from good, was given to the Levites.

@734[14]. The reason the works and ministries of the Levites... are called "warfare," is that the Levites represented the truths of the Church; and Aaron, to whom the Levites were given... for service, represented the Lord as to the good of love, and as to the work of salvation; and as the Lord... regenerates and saves men by means of truths from the Word, and also [by their means] removes the evils and falsities which are from Hell, continually fighting against them, therefore the offices and ministries of the Levites were called "warfare "...

Lewis.; Levi.

@SE 5987. See <Espalier>.

